The source is included verbatim from the upstream repository with the
following LOCAL MODIFICATIONS applied for this project:

1. Vulkan backend — CoherentDeviceLocal heap gate
   File: Backends/Vulkan/VkDevice.cs
   Change: A `CoherentDeviceLocal` memory type is now only preferred when the
   corresponding DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT heap is at least
   1 GiB (MinCoherentDeviceLocalBytes = 1UL << 30). On GPUs where that heap
   is small (e.g. RTX 4070 Ti SUPER exposes only ~214 MB), the upstream
   behaviour of unconditionally preferring that heap caused
   VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY. With this change the allocator falls back
   to a plain HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT buffer, matching the CPU/SIMD path.

   The matching `NewStorageBuffer` allocation logic in VkDevice.cs was also
   updated to honour the new size gate.

No other source files were modified. The rest of the code is unchanged from
the upstream 2.0.0 release.

